KG42.register("source_edge_archive-22dbdf83aef1f3a7d002515a",{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"pricing.local","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-cca2f1628c10ac64","target":"COMP-9ca8822ee86e3e13","source_occurrence_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::V::execution.energy_trade","target_occurrence_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","target_unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Automatic facilitation of energy transactions by an EMTS using a participant's blockchain account. | BMG local trading on the virtual market layer. | BMG trading performed automatically by the EMTS. | Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g03-e023"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"04a2fb4623c3e58abb2ac8f2df68fe6dfb6b340cc5843e1915a1c26dd9d64662","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"For the illustrative simple EMTS, purchasing energy on the microgrid market is conditioned on the local market price falling below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the simple EMTS's maximum price limit. Local trading is conducted only virtually on the blockchain and does not influence the physical delivery of electricity. Scope: BMG local trading on the virtual market layer. Automatic trading requires participant preferences, such as preferred energy sources and price limits. Scope: BMG trading performed automatically by the EMTS. Condition: Automatic trading by the EMTS. The EMTS must have access to its market participant's blockchain account to facilitate energy transactions automatically. Scope: Automatic facilitation of energy transactions by an EMTS using a participant's blockchain account. Condition: Energy transactions are facilitated automatically by the EMTS.","target_definition":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used. A clearing price is determined in every time slot; prices vary with demand, supply and socio-economic characteristics. Scope: BMG stated time-slot pricing design. Condition: When the described time-slot pricing design is used. Energy surplus should lower the microgrid energy price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: There is an energy surplus. A lack of local energy increases the market price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Local energy is lacking. The local energy price may exceed the external grid price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Socio-economic reasons, such as supporting local renewable energy, are considered. The electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Scope: BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. Condition: During this trial, in which the market mechanism was not actively used. Each transaction may have an individual transaction price. Scope: BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. Condition: If the proposed pay-as-you bid order book is used.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"For the illustrative simple EMTS, purchasing energy on the microgrid market is conditioned on the local market price falling below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the simple EMTS's maximum price limit.","expression":"p_{\\mathrm{local}} \u003c p_{\\max} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; b = 1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_R006_buy"],"parameter_refs":["theta_R006_p_local","theta_R006_p_max"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Automatic facilitation of energy transactions by an EMTS using a participant's blockchain account. | BMG local trading on the virtual market layer. | BMG trading performed automatically by the EMTS. | Illustrative simple EMTS purchasing on a microgrid market; not a universal BMG trading rule.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g03-e023"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"pricing.local","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish general microgrid design, the BMG implemented virtual double auction, and the example EMTS; the original undercut statement is recorded as a source statement and is not rewritten on our own into the opposite condition."}});
